er, playing **d7-d5** immediately locks in central control before White potentially plays d4. It gains space and prepares queenside development.\n\nReason:  \nPlaying **P: d7-d5** stakes a strong claim in the center, supports future piece development (especially the c8-bishop and queen), and is a highly principled, high-probability winning strategy at all levels of chess.\n\nAnswer: P: d7-d5"}
