. Between them, **B: c8-d7** is better because it develops a piece without blocking the queen, keeps flexibility in the center, and prepares potential counterplay on the queenside.\n\nReason: Developing the bishop with **B: c8-d7** improves piece activity, avoids blocking the queen, and maintains flexibility in the center and on the queenside. It’s consistent with sound opening principles—developing minor pieces and contesting the center.\n\nAnswer: B: c8-d7'}
